  "liner": {
   "body_md": "Mountain Goats performed at the Bowery Ballroom in New York on March 28, 2011, during their Full Fish Moon Tour [8]. The recommended recording, uploaded by nyctaper, is a matrix mix of soundboard and audience microphones, capturing all 24 songs over 105 minutes [1]. This audio file was originally posted on nyctaper.com [1]. The lineup included John Darnielle on vocals and guitar, Peter Hughes on bass and vocals, Jon Wurster on drums, and Yuval Semo on keyboards and guitar, with Craig Finn joining for vocals [2]. The setlist features several rare tracks, including “Estate Sale Sign,” “High Hawk Season,” “You Were Cool,” “Outer Scorpion Squadron,” “Prowl Great Cain,” and “Plain,” which are noted as firsts in the archive [1]. “Seeing Daylight” and “Family Happiness” are also rare, with only 13 and 7 archived performances respectively [1]. A separate audience recording by Bluesmer, rated 5/5 by one listener, describes the performance as a top-three favorite boot with steady audio and a strong setlist [2][3]. The show is the 153rd of 467 archived performances for the band [4]. Fan art for the event is credited to Maryanne Ventrice [9].",
